+# A run holds its slot only while Godot itself lives: the slot fd is closed in the child (anything Godot starts used to
+# inherit it and keep the slot after Godot was gone), TERM/INT end Godot too (they used to end only this script), and a
+# run is ended after GODOT_MAX_S (default 6 h; 0 = no limit). A Godot started by a Godot that came through here runs at
+# once, without a second slot: its parent holds one and waits for it (2026-11-11: that wait jammed all 14 slots).
